WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.180
SOWMYA KANNAN: Hello.

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:03.010
I'm Sowmya Kannan.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.670
Today I'll be giving you an
overview of the Associate Cloud

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.730
engineer track that is
part of a Career Readiness

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.900
Program from Google Cloud.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.200
In today's presentation, we'll
start with an introduction

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.930
to Google and Google Cloud.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.200
We'll see why businesses
are moving to Google Cloud

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.130
Platform.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.130
I'll briefly discuss the
increasing skills gap

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.090
in the "cloud-first" world and
how you can help your students

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.760
build career skills
by leveraging Google

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.760
Cloud's Associate
Cloud engineer track.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.700
I'll provide an overview
and review the benefits

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.840
of this program and timelines.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.420
I'll also share what
your responsibilities

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.520
would be as a faculty leader.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.620
I'll discuss how
Google Cloud will

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:56.270
assist faculty and students
in completing this program.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:59.660
Coursera and Qwiklabs setup
will be presented next,

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.990
and I'll conclude with the
next steps for you to take.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.450
I'm sure most of you are
aware that Google started

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:08.820
in 1998 in a small garage.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:14.340
Today, Google has more than 70
offices across 50 countries.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.030
For the past 20 years,
Google has been working hard

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.670
to organize the
world's information

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:25.080
and make it universally
accessible and useful.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:29.930
We've created products such as
search, Android, Chrome, Maps,

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:34.370
Play, YouTube, Gmail
and Drive, all now

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:37.520
with over a billion users.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.120
However, it's not
just the scale that's

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.640
interesting about
these products.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.920
What's interesting is
the infrastructure,

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.920
Google's core technology
infrastructure

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:52.920
that we had to build in
order to achieve our mission.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.030
This infrastructure
powers all our products.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:01.190
Google Cloud Platform is a suite
of cloud computing services

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:04.520
that runs on the same
infrastructure used

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:09.060
by Google internally for
its end user products.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.890
So why are businesses moving
to Google Cloud Platform?

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.770
When making this
transition, most companies

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.770
are not just looking at how
they can move their existing

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:22.950
computing to the cloud, or
to reduce costs, and increase

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.230
reliability and security.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:29.950
They are also hoping to
create new opportunities.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:33.430
Google Cloud has been placed
in the leaders quadrant

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.010
by Gartner in 2018.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:40.600
Forester also recognizes
Google as a leader in key areas

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.340
of cloud computing.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.910
More than $1.3
trillion in IT spending

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:49.180
will be directly or indirectly
affected by the shift

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.400
to cloud by 2022.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.860
Adoption of cloud
native applications

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:58.280
will double by 2020.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.680
This accelerated
move towards cloud

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.610
has created a tremendous demand
for qualified professionals

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:07.160
who are proficient in
cloud technologies.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.740
The growth in cloud
adoption has resulted

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.620
in a corresponding increase
in the need for workers

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:15.230
skilled in cloud technologies.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:18.920
So are your students
cloud ready?

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.310
To bridge the skills gap,
we've built an enterprise

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:25.390
ready curriculum leading
up to industry recognized

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.190
certification.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.870
Lead a sprint through the
Associate Cloud engineer

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:32.630
track to empower your
students to succeed

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:35.080
in cloud-related careers.

